# Testing

## Tooling
- `pytest` + `pytest-asyncio` (auto mode via `pyproject.toml`).
- `httpx.AsyncClient` for API tests.
- `FakeLLMProvider` for LLM-dependent tests — no network calls.

## Structure
- `tests/unit/` — service logic with fakes; no DB, no network.
- `tests/integration/` — real DB (testcontainers or SQLite),
  real API routes.

## Naming
`test_<what>_<condition>_<expected>`
Example: `test_extract_with_empty_contract_returns_empty_list`

## Coverage rule
Every public service method: at least one happy-path test and one
error-path test.

## Never
- Network calls in any test.
- `time.sleep()` — use `await asyncio.sleep()` only if timing-critical.
- `assert result` — use `assert result == expected` or
  `assert result is not None`.
- Shared mutable state between tests (use function-scoped fixtures).